{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat AGENTS.md; cat .agents/skills/task-spec/docs/guides/toolkit/execution.md'","aggregated_output":"# Chat qualification fixture\n\nUse the installed task-spec skill at .agents/skills/task-spec/SKILL.md.\nThe version-matched TaskSpec CLI is `bash \"/private/tmp/taskspec-planning-fix-engines/3.10.0/bin/taskspec\"`.\nThis is a fresh conversation: derive current state from artifacts.\nFollow the user request within this repository. Do not spawn agents, commit, publish, or change the installed engine.\n# Execute and recover with TaskMesh\n\nInitialize TaskMesh with `taskspec mesh init` in the authorized host environment\nbefore using it from a coding harness that protects Git metadata. Initialization\nwrites `.git/info/exclude` and creates the repository-local daemon state. Several\ninspection commands also initialize a missing daemon; they are not guaranteed to\nbe filesystem read-only. If the host denies this setup, report that boundary and\nwait for the required authorization. Do not switch tools to repeat the denied write.\n\nInspect `taskspec status <task>`, `taskspec mesh frontier`, and\n`taskspec mesh explain --task <id>`. Ready leaves need a valid HMAC seal.\nUse `taskspec mesh run --initiative <id> --execute` for the eligible native\ninitiative frontier, or `mesh run --task <id> --execute` for one managed task.\nDeclared resources and overlapping writes share the existing concurrency logic.\nA run starts the currently eligible wave; inspect status before requesting later work.\nWithout `--execute`, `mesh run` still creates a run, worktree and lease. Use\n`--dry-run` for a preview; omitting `--execute` is not a preview.\n\nA recipe-managed run follows existing attempts, worktrees, leases, fencing,\ncancellation, and recovery. Per-round artifacts retain executor and eval evidence;\nno separate loop runner is introduced. In supervised mode, passing evals enter\nawaiting_supervision.\n\nNew source worktrees live under `.taskspec/mesh/workspaces/<run>/`, outside Git's\nmetadata directory. Existing recorded workspace paths remain valid. The daemon\nrenews the fenced lease while it owns an active executor; renewal does not extend\nthe signed deadline or refund rounds. If renewal loses authority, execution stops.\nRecognized harness permission-denial results park immediately instead of entering\nanother repair round. Resolve the reported permission boundary before resuming;\nan eval failure and a denied tool action need different recovery decisions.\n\nUse `mesh accept <attempt> --supervised-by <identity> --reason <text>` only with\napplicable supervisor authorization. `finish` reports the human integration route.\nCanonical acceptance receipts may already exist as untracked files in the\nsupervisor checkout. After `finish`, inspect `git status --short` and commit the\nexact receipt files for that run before performing the reported merge. This\npreserves the evidence and avoids Git refusing to overwrite untracked receipts.\nTaskMesh does not perform this user-branch commit or merge.\n\nAfter interruption, read `mesh status`, `mesh watch <run>`, and initiative state.\nUse `mesh resume <run-or-attempt> --execute` only after resolving the recorded blocker.\nResuming does not refund recipe rounds or restart its total deadline. Exhaustion\nrequires reviewed successor work, not silent budget expansion.\n\nOrdinary tasks retain direct `taskspec handoff`. Managed recipes require TaskMesh.\nSupervised adapters and the attested OMP sandbox use the same round controller.\nAutonomous OMP requires the pinned sandbox, fixed provider/model, external host\nattestor, and evaluator trust registry. Each round receives a fresh expiring\ncapability and retains its own signed execution evidence; prior credentials stay\nrevoked. Evals run in the sanitized host environment, and canonical acceptance\nreruns the task proof. Execution attestation does not claim eval isolation.\nAutomatic acceptance evaluation uses the remaining signed deadline; cancellation\nalso stops its evaluator subprocesses. An explicit later supervisor acceptance\ndoes not grant new execution rounds or reset the managed run's deadline.\nCustom required environment contracts and hard token limits refuse before any\nround when their enforcement cannot be established. No silent downgrade occurs.\n\nKeep the authorized task, native plan bundle, immutable snapshots, and applicable\nsource evidence in the Git revision used for the attempt. Mesh creates worktrees\nfrom that revision. Recording files in Git does not replace review or HMAC sealing.\n\nRound evidence distinguishes explicitly routed models from models reported by a\nharness. Unreported defaults remain unknown; comparative qualification requires\nexplicit model and provider identities. Supervised adapters use the harness host\nenvironment; required isolation or hard token enforcement must refuse if unavailable.\n\nRecipe-managed Claude runs with no declared MCP dependencies use restricted\nRead/Edit/Write/Bash tools and an empty MCP configuration. User, project, and\nlocal settings hooks are excluded from that worker context; managed host policy\nstill applies. Explicit route model/provider choices remain authoritative.\nDeclare needed MCP dependencies or provide an explicitly configured adapter.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'bash \"/private/tmp/taskspec-planning-fix-engines/3.10.0/bin/taskspec\" agent-context'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"contract\": \"TaskSpecAgentContext/v1\",\n  \"engine_version\": \"3.10.0\",\n  \"format_version\": 4,\n  \"default_format_version\": 3,\n  \"supported_format_versions\": [\n    1,\n    2,\n    3,\n    4\n  ],\n  \"binary\": \"taskspec\",\n  \"global_options\": {\n    \"--json\": \"wrap command stdout/stderr and exit status in one JSON envelope\",\n    \"--dry-run\": \"prevent supported mutations and report intended action\",\n    \"NO_COLOR\": \"disable ANSI color when present\",\n    \"TASKSPEC_COLOR\": \"0 disables and 1 forces ANSI color\"\n  },\n  \"exit_codes\": {\n    \"0\": \"success\",\n    \"1\": \"validation, gate, eval, or acceptance failure\",\n    \"2\": \"usage error\",\n    \"3\": \"unsupported runtime requirement\"\n  },\n  \"commands\": {\n    \"init\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"creates missing tasks/ and .taskspec/config\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"INIT=OK\",\n        \"INIT=DRY_RUN\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec init [--force]\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--force\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"creates missing tasks/ and .taskspec/config\"\n    },\n    \"setup\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"none\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"SETUP=READY\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec setup | taskspec setup signing [--force] | taskspec setup decompose\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--force\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"none\"\n    },\n    \"setup signing\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"creates or explicitly rotates the repository-private HMAC key\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec setup signing\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"creates or explicitly rotates the repository-private HMAC key\"\n    },\n    \"demo\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"creates and removes an isolated temporary repository\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"DEMO=READY\",\n        \"DEMO=DRY_RUN\",\n        \"DEMO=BLOCKED\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec demo\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"creates and removes an isolated temporary repository\"\n    },\n    \"example\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"writes one installed canonical example non-clobberingly; --force replaces and --dry-run writes nothing\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"EXAMPLE=WRITTEN\",\n        \"EXAMPLE=DRY_RUN\",\n        \"EXAMPLE=REFUSED\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec example task-plan --out <file> [--force]\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--force\",\n        \"--out\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"writes one installed canonical example non-clobberingly; --force replaces and --dry-run writes nothing\\nExamples: task-plan, intent, recipe, incident, release-evidence. Use taskspec help example <kind>.\"\n    },\n    \"new\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"creates one Task-Spec scaffold and derived state\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec new [--format 3|4] [--status ready|blocked] [--queue] <slug> <XS|S|M|L|XL|XXL> [agent] [source-note]\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--format\",\n        \"--queue\",\n        \"--status\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"creates one Task-Spec scaffold and derived state\"\n    },\n    \"plan\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"none\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"TASK_PLAN=OK\",\n        \"TASK_PLAN=INVALID\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec plan --manifest <TaskPlan.yaml>\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--manifest\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"none\"\n    },\n    \"batch\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"creates declared Task-Spec scaffolds; --dry-run writes nothing\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"TASK_BATCH=OK\",\n        \"TASK_BATCH=DRY_RUN\",\n        \"TASK_BATCH=REFUSED\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec batch --plan <TaskPlan.yaml> | taskspec batch --intent-file <file> --effort <size>\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--effort\",\n        \"--intent-file\",\n        \"--plan\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"creates declared Task-Spec scaffolds; --dry-run writes nothing\"\n    },\n    \"migrate\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"atomically upgrades one explicitly named legacy task under the task-state lock\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec migrate <task-spec>\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"atomically upgrades one explicitly named legacy task under the task-state lock\"\n    },\n    \"validate\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"refreshes deterministic derived state unless --no-state\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec validate [--no-state] <task-spec>\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--no-state\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"refreshes deterministic derived state unless --no-state\"\n    },\n    \"dod\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"none\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"DOD=COMPLETE\",\n        \"DOD=GAPS\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec dod <task-spec>\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"none\"\n    },\n    \"gate\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"executes task evals; --stamp additionally writes the sign-off envelope\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"TIER=1\",\n        \"TIER=2\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec gate [--stamp] [--require-tier1] <task-spec>\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--require-tier\",\n        \"--stamp\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"executes task evals; --stamp additionally writes the sign-off envelope\"\n    },\n    \"handoff\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"stdout is read-only; --out writes non-clobberingly unless --force\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"HANDOFF=WRITTEN\",\n        \"HANDOFF=INVALID\",\n        \"HANDOFF=REFUSED\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec handoff <task-spec> --backend <token> [--out <file>] [--attempt-id <uuid>]\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--attempt-id\",\n        \"--backend\",\n        \"--out\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"stdout is read-only; --out writes non-clobberingly unless --force\"\n    },\n    \"run\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"runs declared eval commands in the task workspace\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec run [--ci] <task-spec>\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--ci\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"runs declared eval commands in the task workspace\"\n    },\n    \"accept\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"executes acceptance evals; --stamp additionally writes AcceptanceRecord/v1 and the acceptance envelope\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"ACCEPTED=1\",\n        \"ACCEPTED=0\",\n        \"ACCEPTANCE_FAILURE=<code>\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec accept [--stamp] [--handoff <file>] [receipt flags] <task-spec>\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--handoff\",\n        \"--stamp\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"executes acceptance evals; --stamp additionally writes AcceptanceRecord/v1 and the acceptance envelope\"\n    },\n    \"author-doctor\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"none\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"AUTHOR_DOCTOR=READY\",\n        \"AUTHOR_DOCTOR=INVALID\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec author-doctor <task-spec>\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"none\"\n    },\n    \"holdout\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"seal/run may write descriptor or receipt; verify is read-only\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"HOLDOUT=SEALED\",\n        \"HOLDOUT=VERIFIED\",\n        \"HOLDOUT=INVALID\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec holdout seal|verify|run ...\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"seal/run may write descriptor or receipt; verify is read-only\"\n    },\n    \"receipt\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"creator/sign commands write explicit receipt paths; validate is read-only\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"RECEIPT=WRITTEN\",\n        \"RECEIPT=SIGNED\",\n        \"RECEIPT=INVALID\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec receipt validate|sign|engine|environment|evaluation|graded|human ...\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"creator/sign commands write explicit receipt paths; validate is read-only\"\n    },\n    \"eval-audit\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"uses temporary git worktrees; optional report path\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"EVAL_AUDIT=INVALID\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec eval-audit <task-spec> --baseline <git-ref> [--mutations <matrix>] [--repeat N]\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--baseline\",\n        \"--mutations\",\n        \"--repeat\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"uses temporary git worktrees; optional report path\"\n    },\n    \"identity\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"init/sign/revoke write explicit files; verify is read-only\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"IDENTITY=READY\",\n        \"IDENTITY=SIGNED\",\n        \"IDENTITY=VERIFIED\",\n        \"IDENTITY=REVOKED\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec identity init|sign|verify|revoke ...\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"init/sign/revoke write explicit files; verify is read-only\"\n    },\n    \"evidence\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"run writes an explicit evidence directory; validate/plan are read-only\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"ENGINE_MATRIX=VALID\",\n        \"ENGINE_MATRIX=INVALID\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec evidence validate|plan|run <EngineMatrix.json> ...\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"run writes an explicit evidence directory; validate/plan are read-only\"\n    },\n    \"bridge\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"export writes only with --out; validate is read-only\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"BRIDGE=VALID\",\n        \"BRIDGE=INVALID\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec bridge export|validate ...\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"export writes only with --out; validate is read-only\"\n    },\n    \"dsse\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"export writes only to --out; verify is read-only\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"DSSE=EXPORTED\",\n        \"DSSE=VERIFIED\",\n        \"DSSE=INVALID\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec dsse export|verify ...\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"export writes only to --out; verify is read-only\"\n    },\n    \"mcp\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"read-only stdio server\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec mcp\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"read-only stdio server\"\n    },\n    \"mesh\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"optional repository-local control plane; run/cancel/resume/accept/finish/setup mutate disposable mesh state while canonical acceptance still calls Task-Spec\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"MESH_WATCH_READY\",\n        \"MESH_SUPERVISED_ACCEPTED\",\n        \"MESH_FINISHED\",\n        \"TASKMESH_ERROR=<code>\",\n        \"TASKMESH_DRY_RUN\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec mesh <init|doctor|serve|frontier|run|status|watch|explain|cancel|resume|accept|finish|adapters|setup|mcp> ... | taskspec mesh run --initiative <id> [--execute]\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--execute\",\n        \"--initiative\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"optional repository-local control plane; run/cancel/resume/accept/finish/setup mutate disposable mesh state while canonical acceptance still calls Task-Spec\"\n    },\n    \"ready\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"none\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec ready [--all] [filters]\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--all\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"none\"\n    },\n    \"graph\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"none; TaskGraphView/v1 is derived from Markdown and Git\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"GRAPH=<digest>\",\n        \"GRAPH=INVALID\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec graph [--task <id>] [--check] [--mermaid] [--json] | taskspec graph --initiative <id> --view tasks|capabilities\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--check\",\n        \"--initiative\",\n        \"--json\",\n    